02. Audit Retention Policies

This is the second major part of Audit after Search.

The most important thing to understand is:

🔎 Audit Search tells you what happened.
📜 Audit Retention Policy determines how long the audit evidence is kept.

That distinction should become automatic in your mind.

Microsoft currently documents Audit Log Retention Policies as an Audit (Premium) capability. 
They allow you to define how long qualifying audit records are retained, with retention possible up 
to 10 years when the required licensing is in place



🧠 1. First understand the problem

Imagine your company has this event:

👤 Rahul downloaded confidential financial files on 13 August 2026.

An audit record is generated:

👤 Rahul
      ↓
📂 SharePoint
      ↓
📥 File download
      ↓
📝 Audit Record

You investigate it today:

13 Aug 2026 → Audit Search → Record found

Good.

But suppose the company comes back 2 years later and asks:

"What did Rahul do on 13 August 2026?"

If the audit record has already expired, Search cannot magically recover it.

Therefore:

⚙️ Activity happens
        ↓
📝 Audit Record
        ↓
📜 Retention Policy
        ↓
🗄️ Record retained for required period
        ↓
🔎 Future investigation
🎯 The purpose of an Audit Retention Policy:

Keep the audit evidence for the period required by the organization's security, compliance, legal, or investigation requirements.

