🧩 4. What exactly can we target with an Audit Retention Policy?

This is where Audit Retention Policies become powerful.

Microsoft currently allows custom audit retention policies to be based on criteria including:

👤 Users

Specific users or all users.

☁️ Microsoft service / workload

For example, activities occurring in a particular Microsoft service.

🏷️ Record type

A specific type of audit record.

⚙️ Activity

If you select a single record type, you can further select specific activities.

⏳ Duration

How long matching audit records should be retained.

🔢 Priority

Which policy takes precedence when multiple policies match.

👤 5. Users — WHO?

Suppose your organization has:

10,000 employees

But your security team considers these users especially important:

🔐 Global Administrators
🔐 Security Administrators
🧑‍💼 Compliance Administrators
💰 Finance executives
👨‍💼 C-level executives
🛡️ Security investigation accounts

You might have a requirement such as:

"Keep audit records associated with privileged users for a longer period."

That is where user-scoped retention becomes useful.

Conceptually:
All users
   │
   ├── Normal users → standard retention
   │
   └── Critical users
           ↓
      longer retention

But don't blindly create a policy for every important employee.

You should have a business/security requirement for doing so.

☁️ 6. Service / Workload

Suppose your organization has a requirement:

"SharePoint activity must be available for long-term investigation."

You can design retention around the relevant audit records/workload.

Think:

Microsoft 365
      │
      ├── Exchange
      ├── SharePoint
      ├── OneDrive
      ├── Teams
      ├── Entra ID
      ├── Power Platform
      └── Other services

You don't necessarily need the same retention requirement for every workload.

🏷️ 7. Record Type

This connects directly to what we learned earlier.

Remember:

Record Type = type/classification of the audit record.

A retention policy can target particular record types.

For example, conceptually:

"Retain a particular category of administrative/security audit records longer."

So your mental connection should now be:

📝 Audit Record
