I want you to keep one nuance in mind:

Don't think that every audit record simply gets its retention period from the policy with the longest duration.

Policy matching and precedence matter, and Microsoft determines the audit item's lifetime through the auditing pipeline based on applicable licensing and retention policies. Changes to licensing/policies affect expiration behavior after updating; they don't recover already-expired data.

So when you design policies, scope + priority + licensing all matter.

